# VTID-03730 — commands actually run.

# --- Discovery -----------------------------------------------------------
# Found the exact checklist of files that must agree by following the
# VTID-03681 precedent (the pt/pl expansion), which documents itself as the
# authoritative "when adding a language, these tables must all be updated
# together" note across 8 files.

grep -rln "VTID-03681" services/gateway/src
#   -> orb/live/config.ts, orb/live/instruction/live-system-instruction.ts,
#      routes/orb-live.ts, services/decision-contract/types.ts,
#      orb/live/voice/live-api-voice.ts, orb/live/voice/voice-mapping.ts,
#      orb/live/upstream/cascaded-config.ts, orb/instruction/greeting-pools.ts

grep -n "POLLY_VOICES\|POLLY_UNSUPPORTED_LANGS" -A 15 \
  services/gateway/src/services/tts/polly.ts
#   -> POLLY_UNSUPPORTED_LANGS = new Set(['sr']) only; POLLY_VOICES had no
#      'tr' entry — a genuine gap, not a documented "unsupported" language.

# --- Edits -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Added a `tr` entry to every table the VTID-03681 note names as load-bearing:
#   1. SUPPORTED_LIVE_LANGUAGES (orb/live/config.ts)
#   2. languageNames map (orb/live/instruction/live-system-instruction.ts)
#   3-5. two languageNames maps + nameToCode reverse map (routes/orb-live.ts)
#   6. SupportedLanguage / SUPPORTED_LANGUAGES invariant (decision-contract/types.ts)
#   7. LIVE_API_VOICE_FALLBACKS (orb/live/voice/live-api-voice.ts)
#   8. LIVE_LANGUAGE_VOICE_FALLBACKS / GEMINI_TTS_VOICE_FALLBACKS /
#      NEURAL2_TTS_VOICE_FALLBACKS (orb/live/voice/voice-mapping.ts) —
#      NEURAL2_ENABLED_LANGUAGES_FALLBACK deliberately left untouched,
#      matching the pt/pl precedent (single seeded DB array row)
#   9. SHORT_GAP_GREETING_PHRASES (orb/instruction/greeting-pools.ts) — 8
#      informal-register Turkish phrases
#   10. TRANSCRIBE_LANGUAGE_CODES (orb/live/upstream/cascaded-config.ts) — tr-TR
#   11. POLLY_VOICES (services/tts/polly.ts) — Filiz/standard/tr-TR
#       (UNVERIFIED against the live Polly API — no AWS credentials in this
#       session; also added to scripts/tts/verify-polly-voices.ts for the
#       next session that has them)
#
# Deliberately did NOT add a Turkish entry to NOVA_VOICES
# (orb/live/voice/nova-sonic-voice.ts) — unlike the tables above, these ids
# are sent to the REAL live Nova/Bedrock API, and the only precedent for
# adding one (`pt` -> `carolina`) was confirmed live under VTID-03672. No
# live Nova credentials here to confirm a Turkish id the same way, so `tr`
# correctly falls through to null -> the documented `tina` substitution,
# same as ru/pl/ar/zh/sr.

# --- Rebase onto latest main, and a real course correction --------------------
#
# On first push, `git push -u origin claude/vitanaland-language-expansion-fivoly`
# reported "new branch" (the prior VTID-03723/03729 PRs on this same branch
# name had already merged and their remote branch was deleted) and the
# resulting PR showed mergeable_state:"dirty", 9 commits, 73 files — this
# branch's LOCAL history still carried the old, already-merged VTID-03723/
# VTID-03729 commits (never rebased after those PRs merged), duplicating
# content `main` already had under different squash-merge SHAs.

git fetch origin main
git log --oneline origin/main -5
#   -> origin/main HEAD (c9300f6d) already contains VTID-03729 and VTID-03723
#      as its own commits — confirming the branch's local copies were stale,
#      redundant history, not genuinely unmerged work.

git log --oneline origin/main | grep -iE "turkish|VTID-037(1[5-9]|2[0-9])"
#   -> surfaced VTID-03719 (#3175, "add Turkish Polly voice + CJK-aware
#      audio-timing pacing bounds"), already merged to main — a live-verified
#      Burcu/neural Polly voice for tr that this session did not know about
#      when it wrote its own unverified Filiz/standard guess.

git show origin/main:services/gateway/src/orb/live/config.ts | grep -A11 "SUPPORTED_LIVE_LANGUAGES: string\[\]"
#   -> confirms `tr` is STILL absent from the gate on main — VTID-03719 fixed
#      only the Polly voice table, not the session-start gate, so this VTID's
#      core defect is still real and still needed.

git show b44f54fd --stat
#   -> VTID-03719's file list: services/tts/polly.ts +
#      scripts/tts/verify-cascade-audio-timing.ts + tests only. Confirms none
#      of the other 8 must-agree tables were touched by it.

for f in orb/instruction/greeting-pools.ts services/decision-contract/types.ts \
         orb/live/instruction/live-system-instruction.ts orb/live/voice/voice-mapping.ts \
         orb/live/voice/live-api-voice.ts orb/live/voice/nova-sonic-voice.ts \
         services/voice-lab/nova-sonic-test-runner.ts; do
  git show origin/main:services/gateway/src/$f | grep -c "'tr'\|tr:"
done
#   -> 0 for every file: confirms the remaining 7 tables (all but polly.ts)
#      are genuinely still missing tr on main, exactly as originally planned.

# Fix: reset the branch to origin/main, keep ONLY the genuinely unmerged
# Turkish-support commit, cherry-pick it on top.

git checkout -B claude/vitanaland-language-expansion-fivoly origin/main
git cherry-pick <original-commit-sha>
#   -> 2 conflicts, both expected and both in favor of main:
#      services/gateway/src/services/tts/polly.ts and
#      services/gateway/test/tts/polly-provider.test.ts — main's version
#      (Burcu/neural, already covering `tr` in every list/assertion) is
#      strictly better than this session's unverified Filiz/standard guess.
#      Resolved via `git checkout --ours` on both (keep main's content,
#      discard this branch's), `git add`, `git cherry-pick --continue`.
#      Every other file (config.ts, live-system-instruction.ts, orb-live.ts,
#      decision-contract/types.ts, voice-mapping.ts, live-api-voice.ts,
#      greeting-pools.ts, cascaded-config.ts, nova-sonic-test-runner.ts, and
#      all their tests) auto-merged cleanly — genuinely new, non-overlapping
#      content.

# Also corrected scripts/tts/verify-polly-voices.ts's EXPECTED.tr entry by
# hand afterward (Filiz/standard -> Burcu/neural) — it isn't part of any
# VTID-03719 file and so wasn't touched by the cherry-pick/conflict, but was
# still carrying this session's original wrong guess.

